1
00:05:18,947 --> 00:05:24,947
When Shade's good, she's very good. But when Trudi's bad, she's better.

2
00:10:37,894 --> 00:10:43,894
Gas Food Lodging is a drama, romance film directed by Allison Anders.

3
00:15:56,842 --> 00:16:02,842
Nora, a single mother raising two teenage daughters, Shade and Trudi, waits
tables at a truck-stop diner in a small New Mexico town.

4
00:21:15,789 --> 00:21:21,789
The beautiful and rebellious Trudi drops out of school and gets a job alongside Nora,
while the younger Shade whittles away her time at Spanish movie matinees.

5
00:26:34,736 --> 00:26:40,736
Their lives are turned upside down when Trudi becomes
pregnant and the girls' absent father returns.

6
00:31:53,684 --> 00:31:59,684
Nora, played by Brooke Adams.

7
00:37:12,631 --> 00:37:18,631
Trudi, played by Ione Skye.

8
00:42:31,578 --> 00:42:37,578
Shade, played by Fairuza Balk.

9
00:47:50,526 --> 00:47:56,526
John Evans, played by James Brolin.

10
00:53:09,473 --> 00:53:15,473
Dank, played by Robert Knepper.

11
00:58:28,421 --> 00:58:34,421
Hamlet, played by David Lansbury.

12
01:03:47,368 --> 01:03:53,368
Gas Food Lodging is a 1992 American drama film written and directed by Allison
Anders, based on the novel Don't Look and It Won't Hurt by Richard Peck.

13
01:09:06,315 --> 01:09:12,315
Starring Brooke Adams, Ione Skye, and Fairuza Balk, the film follows a waitress trying to find romance
while raising two daughters in a trailer park in a small desert town in New Mexico.

14
01:14:25,263 --> 01:14:31,263
Gas Food Lodging premiered at the Sundance Film Festival in January 1992, where it was nominated for the Grand Jury Prize, and was
screened at the 42nd Berlin International Film Festival on February 24, 1992, where it was nominated for the Golden Bear.

15
01:19:44,210 --> 01:19:50,210
The film was theatrically released in the United States
on July 10, 1992, to critical acclaim.

16
01:25:03,157 --> 01:25:09,157
At the 8th Independent Spirit Awards, Balk won for Best Female Lead, while the film earned nominations in four other
categories, Best Film, Best Director, and Best Screenplay for Anders, and Best Supporting Female for Adams.

17
01:30:22,105 --> 01:30:28,105
The film explores themes of sibling relationship, waitress,
parent child relationship, new mexico, diner.

18
01:35:41,052 --> 01:35:47,052
The tone is emotional.
